    "content_en": "The Denomination of Origin Ribera del Guadiana covers six subzones in Extremadura, including Tierra de Barros and Matanegra. Predominant soils are clay and calcareous, favoring slow grape maturation. Biochemically, this environment promotes high anthocyanin concentration and stable tannins in varieties like local Tempranillo (Tinto Fino) and the autochthonous Pardina. Enologically, this allows wines with solid structure, balanced acidity, and aging potential.",
