    "content_en": "The D.O.P. Cariñena in Aragon is defined by its unique terroir of alluvial stony soils and pebbles. This geological composition ensures excellent drainage and high heat retention during the day, which is crucial for the homonymous variety (Garnacha Tinta). Biochemically, these conditions induce advanced phenolic maturity, resulting in grapes with thicker cell walls and higher concentrations of stable anthocyanins and tannins. Historically, old vineyards on slopes ensure low yields that enhance aromatic concentration.",
