    "content_en": "D.O. Arribes is characterized by its granitic canyon geography along the international Duero, with vertiginous terraces maximizing solar exposure and phenolic ripening. Unique biodiversity documented by Juan García and Bruñal influences soil microbiology, reducing pests and favoring terroir expression. Biochemically, poor granitic soils induce moderate water stress, concentrating sugars and malic acids, resulting in high-acidity whites and structured-tannin reds.",
