    "id": "nuevo_mundo_oregon_willamette_dundee_hills",
    "standard": "WSET3",
    "category_es": "Nuevo Mundo & Terruño",
    "category_en": "Enology & Terroir",
    "badge_color": "amber",
    "title_es": "Oregon: Dundee Hills y los Suelos Rojos de Jory: Mecanismo y Relevancia Enológica",
    "title_en": "Oregon: Dundee Hills and the Red Jory Soils: Mechanism and Enological Significance",
    "summary_es": "Los suelos rojos de Jory, derivados de basalto volcánico meteorizado, confieren acidez natural y estructura fenólica equilibrada al Pinot Noir del Valle Willamette.",
    "summary_en": "Red Jory soils, derived from weathered volcanic basalt, impart natural acidity and balanced phenolic structure to Willamette Valley Pinot Noir.",
    "content_es": "Los suelos Jory, característicos de Dundee Hills, son basalto volcánico meteorizado con alto contenido en hierro y arcilla. Esta composición química promueve un drenaje excepcional que limita el vigor vegetativo del viñedo, forzando a la vid a desarrollar raíces profundas y concentrar compuestos fenólicos en los racimos. Enológica y sensorialmente, esto se traduce en vinos de Pinot Noir con acidez natural elevada, taninos finos y una estructura mineral compleja.\n\nEl microclima protegido por la sombra de lluvia de las Coast Ranges modera las temperaturas, ralentizando la maduración. Este estrés hídrico controlado preserva los ácidos málicos y permite el desarrollo de aromas primarios frutales (cereza, fresa) combinados con notas terciarias terrosas típicas del basalto.",
    "content_en": "Jory soils, characteristic of Dundee Hills, are weathered volcanic basalt with high iron and clay content. This chemical composition promotes exceptional drainage that limits vineyard vegetative vigor, forcing the vine to develop deep roots and concentrate phenolic compounds in the berries. Enologically and sensorially, this translates into Pinot Noir wines with elevated natural acidity, fine tannins, and a complex mineral structure.\n\nThe microclimate protected by the rain shadow of the Coast Ranges moderates temperatures, slowing ripening. This controlled water stress preserves malic acids and allows the development of primary fruity aromas (cherry, strawberry) combined with tertiary earthy notes typical of basalt.",
    "key_takeaways_es": [
      "El basalto rojizo mejora el drenaje y reduce el vigor vegetativo de la vid.",
      "La sombra de lluvia preserva la acidez natural y los aromas frutales primarios.",
      "Perfil sensorial elegante con notas minerales y estructura fenólica equilibrada."
    ],
    "key_takeaways_en": [
      "Red basalt improves drainage and reduces vine vegetative vigor.",
      "Rain shadow preserves natural acidity and primary fruit aromas.",
      "Elegant sensory profile with mineral notes and balanced phenolic structure."
    ],
    "related_grapes": [
      "Pinot Noir",
      "Chardonnay"
    ],
    "related_regions": [
      "Dundee Hills",
      "Willamette Valley"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "nuevo mundo oregon willamette dundee hills",
      "enologia",
      "terruño"
    ]
