    "content_en": "The horseshoe geography of Apalta Valley protects the zone from cold southern winds, allowing for slow and balanced maturation. Nutrient-poor granitic soils induce moderate water stress, concentrating sugars and polyphenols in Carménère grapes. Enologically, this results in wines with soft yet structured tannins, medium acidity, and notes of ripe black fruits like black plum and roasted coffee, distinctive of the Chilean style.",
