    "content_en": "The Bandol terroir is defined by its 'restanques', stone amphitheaters that protect vines from wind and retain heat, crucial for Mourvèdre phenolic maturity. Sandstone and marl soils with marine fossils contribute minerality and deep drainage, limiting vegetative vigor and concentrating phenolic compounds. The wine biochemistry results in high-structure tannins and stable color, typical of the variety.",
